                    "Analyzing the ESI-MS data, the base peak at m/z 134.10955 with intensity 100% is likely [M+H]+. Subtracting the proton mass (1.00728) gives M = 133.10227. The isotope pattern shows M+1 at 10.98% intensity, which follows the rule of thumb: %M+1 ≈ 1.1% x number of carbons. This suggests 10.98/1.1 ≈ 10 carbons (or close to it). For C10H13N: exact mass = 10(12.0) + 13(1.008) + 14.007 = 147.105 (too high). For C9H11N: exact mass = 9(12.0107) + 11(1.00783) + 14.0067 = 133.10913, which matches within 5 ppm of our observed 133.10227. The nitrogen rule states that odd molecular mass suggests odd number of nitrogens - 133 is odd, so 1 nitrogen is consistent. Therefore, C9H11N.": 0.0,
